       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The current FDA label doesn't support that claim.\n\n- **Immediate-release metformin:** the labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day, with a usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. Extended-release is capped at 2,000 mg/day.\n- **This order:** 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the labeled maximum. A 1700 mg single dose is also well above the per-dose limit.\n\nThis isn't a case where an exception would apply. The dose risks serious harm, mainly lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum)\n- 1000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals\n- Another dose within label limits\n\nIf you think a dose above the label is clinically needed, please discuss it with pharmacy or the attending. They can then place or authorize the order through the appropriate channel."
      }
